  (20092,'pc-l10',1,'grammar','SUMMARY OF PRONOUNS AND MARKERS','The chart below is a summary of all the I, II, and III Class personal pronouns, markers, and general pronouns you have now learned.

### Personal Pronouns
| I CLASS | II CLASS | III CLASS | III CLASS (L/D/B) |
|:--------|:---------|:----------|:------------------|
| akó     | nákon    | ákon      | ha akon           |
| ikáw/ka | nímo     | ímo       | ha ímo            |
| hiyá    | níya     | íya       | ha íya            |
| kitá    | nátòn    | áton      | ha áton           |
| kamí    | námon    | ámon      | ha ámon           |
| kamó    | niyo     | íyo       | ha inyo           |
| hirá    | nira     | ira       | ha ira            |

### Markers
| Marker Type                  | w/Proper Nouns | w/Common Nouns |
|:-----------------------------|:---------------|:---------------|
| Subject                      | hi             | an             |
| Plural Subject               | hira           | an mga         |
| Possessive/Object            | kan            | han/hin        |
| Plural Possessive/Object     | kan ngan kan   | han mga/hin mga |
| Location/Direction/Beneficiary | ha             | ha mga         |

### General Pronouns (Demonstratives & Adverbs of Place)
| Type                  | Near Speaker | Near Listener | Far   |
|:----------------------|:-------------|:--------------|:------|
| Demonstrative Pronoun | iní          | iton          | adto  |
| Demonstrative (han/hin) | hini         | hiton         | hadto |
| Adverb of Place       | dínhi/didi   | dida          | didto |
',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20093,'pc-l10',2,'grammar','Ma-Actor Focus Formula','In the previous lesson you learned the formula for ma-actor focus.','Ma- Verb + I Cl Actor + II Cl Object + III Cl L/D/B',null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20094,'pc-l10',3,'assessment','Review test — pass to continue',null,null,'production','type','none','both',0.8,true,null),
  (20095,'pc-l11',1,'grammar','Nga Linker','You have already used the NGA linker with the general pronouns to "link" the pronoun with a noun.
For example:

| Waray | English |
|---|---|
| ini nga bata | this child |
| hini nga balay | of this house |
| iton nga bukad | that flower |
| hiton nga kanto | of that corner |
| adto nga lagas | that old person |
| hadto nga kahoy | of that tree |

The NGA linker is used between words that are joined together -- usually a noun and its modifier (or adjective).
Example:

| Waray | English |
|---|---|
| hataas nga babaye | tall woman |
| matambok nga nanay | fat mother |
| makusog nga lalake | strong man |
| matam-is nga mangga | sweet mango |
| maashum nga prutas | sour fruit |
| matab-ang nga sabaw | tasteless soup |
| ini nga bugto | this brother |
| daku nga balay | big house |
| adto nga lagas | that old person |',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20096,'pc-l11',2,'grammar','Descriptive Words in Equational Sentences','When descriptive words which use the nga linker like the above are used in equational sentences, the word order is as follows:

| Waray | English |
|---|---|
| Hataas nga babaye hi Ruth. | Ruth is a tall woman. |
| Matambok nga lalake hi George. | George is a fat man. |
| Malipayon nga tawo hi Paul. | Paul is a happy person |
| Daragita nga babaye an bugto ni Jess. | Jess'' sister is a young girl. |
| Buotan nga tawo an nanay ni Suzie. | Suzie''s mother is a nice person. |','Descriptive word + nga + noun + I CI Marker + rest...',null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20097,'pc-l11',3,'grammar','Nga Linker with I Class Personal/General Pronouns','When I Class Personal Pronouns or I Class General Pronouns are used, they come between the descriptive word and the nga. The personal pronouns, however, are not usually contracted. The nga remains in its full form.

| Waray | English |
|---|---|
| Makusog hiya nga lalake. | He is a strong man. |
| Hubya hira nga mga maestra. | They are lazy teachers. |
| Habubo kami nga mga misyonero. | We(excl) missionaries are short. |
| Kapoy kamo nga mga asawa. | You(pl) wives are tired. |
| Padlas ini nga tawo. | This person is crazy. |
| Maupay iton nga babaye. | That woman is pretty. |
| Madig-on adto nga bangko. | That chair "over there" is strong. |','Descriptive word + I CI Per Pro/1 CI Gen Pro + nga + noun + rest',null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20098,'pc-l11',4,'vocab','Also in this lesson',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20099,'pc-l11',5,'vocab',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20100,'pc-l11',6,'drill',null,null,null,'recognition','mc','peek',null,null,null,null),
  (20101,'pc-l11',7,'drill',null,null,null,'production','voice','none','both',null,null,null),
  (20102,'pc-l11',8,'drill',null,null,null,'production','type','none','both',null,null,null),
  (20103,'pc-l11',9,'assessment','Checkpoint — pass to continue',null,null,'production','type','none','both',0.8,true,null),
  (20104,'pc-l12',1,'grammar','Particles - question word ba','There are several important Waray particles which are commonly used in sentences. In this lesson you will learn one of the most important -- the question word ba.

**BA -- question word**

The particle **ba** when added in a sentence makes it a QUESTION.

The particle **ba** is usually placed in the sentence after the full word.','First Full Word + ba + rest of the sentence',null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20105,'pc-l12',2,'grammar','Ba in ma-actor focus','In a ma-actor focus question, the **ba** also follows the first full word of the sentence. The formula is the same.','First Full Word + ba + rest of the sentence',null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20106,'pc-l12',3,'grammar','Ka+ba','There is an exception to the rule above. When the short form of the pronoun **ikaw** (the pronoun **ka**) is used with the question word **ba**, then **ka** will come before **ba**. This short form of the pronoun **ikaw**, or **ka**, is a VIP word. It usually comes before other particles that you will learn.','First Full Word + ka + ba + rest of the sentence',null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20107,'pc-l12',4,'vocab',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,'The names Jesus, Jesu Kristo, and Satanas take a proper noun marker -- si, ni, or kang. (They are names.) The titles Ginoo, Diyos, and yawa take a common noun marker - an or ha. (They are titles only.)

| Nominative | Genitive | Oblique |
|---|---|---|
| Hi Jesús | ni Jesus | kan Jesus |
| Hi Jésu Krísto | ni Jesu Kristo | kan Jesu Kristo |
| hi Satanás | ni Satanas | kan Satanas |
| An Ginóo | ha Ginoo | |
| An Diyos | ha Diyos | |
| an yáwa | ha yawa | |'),
