  (20111,'pc-l12',8,'drill','Examples',null,null,'recognition','mc','peek',null,null,null,null),
  (20112,'pc-l12',9,'drill',null,null,null,'production','voice','none','both',null,null,null),
  (20113,'pc-l12',10,'drill',null,null,null,'production','type','none','both',null,null,null),
  (20114,'pc-l12',11,'assessment','Checkpoint — pass to continue',null,null,'production','type','none','both',0.8,true,null),
  (20115,'pc-l13',1,'grammar','Particles - na and pa','The small particles na and pa are often confusing to non Filipino speakers of Waray. However, if you learn how to correctly use them and practice them, you will not be confused.

NA -- means "now" or "already"
Na shows that the action is being done now, or that the action has already been done.

PA -- means "still" or "yet"
Pa shows that the action is still being done, or that the action has not yet begun.

The na or pa is placed after the first full word of the sentence. (except with ka) If other particles are also used, the na/pa always come FIRST. They are VIP Particles.',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20116,'pc-l13',2,'grammar','Na',null,'First Full Word + na + rest of the sentence',null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20117,'pc-l13',3,'grammar','Pa',null,'First Full Word + pa + rest of the sentence',null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20118,'pc-l13',4,'grammar','ka + na/pa','The same exception is true for na and pa when the short pronoun KA is used. The na or pa will follow the ka. It is more VIP than na and pa.','First full word + ka + na/pa + rest of the sentence',null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20119,'pc-l13',5,'grammar','na/pa + ba','Many times na and pa are used with the question word ba. When this occurs, the ba follows the na/pa. When short pronoun ka is used, it again always comes before the particles. It is the VIP word.','When ka is not used: First full word + na/pa + ba + rest of the sentence
When ka is used: First full word + ka + na/pa + ba + rest of the sentence',null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20120,'pc-l13',6,'grammar','Summary Formula','This may seem very complicated right now. The correct word order is the most difficult thing. Maybe the following summary formula will help you. Remember the VIP words come first. The VIP Pronoun ka always comes before any particles. The VIP Particles na/pa always are the first particles in the sentence.','First full word + ka + na/pa + ba + other particles + rest...',null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20121,'pc-l13',7,'vocab',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
