  (20130,'pc-l13',16,'drill',null,null,null,'production','type','none','both',null,null,'The Waray word for "or" is simply o.'),
  (20131,'pc-l13',17,'assessment','Checkpoint — pass to continue',null,null,'production','type','none','both',0.8,true,null),
  (20132,'pc-l14',1,'grammar','Particles—liwat / gihapon','In the last lesson you learned the particles ba, na, and pa. These are very important particles for you to know. But there are several others also. In this lesson you will learn how to use the particle liwat / gihapon -- means "also," "too," or "again"

Like the particles in the previous lesson, the particle liwat also is placed in the sentence after the first full word. If there is also a particle na/pa and/or ba, the liwat/gihapon follow them.

`First Full Word (+ na/pa + ba) + liwat/gihapon + rest...`

Thus, the particles liwat/gihapon precede the I Class words (I Class Personal, General Pronouns, and markers).

`First full word + (ka) + liwat/gihapon + I CI Words`',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20133,'pc-l14',2,'vocab',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20134,'pc-l14',3,'drill',null,null,null,'recognition','mc','peek',null,null,null,null),
  (20135,'pc-l14',4,'drill','Examples',null,null,'recognition','mc','peek',null,null,null,'The context will usually determine the appropriate meaning.'),
  (20136,'pc-l14',5,'drill','Examples',null,null,'recognition','mc','peek',null,null,null,'The ba question word is most often omitted and just understood in a liwat question. The inflection of the voice and the context shows whether it is a statement or question.'),
  (20137,'pc-l14',6,'drill',null,null,null,'recognition','cloze','peek',null,null,null,null),
