  (20205,'pc-l21',1,'grammar','Negating mag- Actor Focus Sentences with waray, diri, and ayaw','In the past lessons you learned how to negate mag-actor focus sentences. In this lesson you will review the word order used in negation of an actor focus sentence. You will also learn some new mag-verbs.',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20206,'pc-l21',2,'grammar','Waray/Diri with I Class Personal Pronouns','In the following examples, the waray is used to refer to PAST and PRESENT action, while diri is used to refer to FUTURE action. With both past action or future action, the mag- future tense of the verb is always used when negating.',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20207,'pc-l21',3,'grammar','Waray/Diri with I Class General Pronouns and I Class Markers','Observe the following mag-actor focus which use I Class General Pronouns or I Class Markers.',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20208,'pc-l21',4,'grammar','Ayaw Command Negator in Mag-actor focus','In the Mag-Actor Focus, the ayaw is followed by the prefix pag- with the verb root.','Ayaw + pag-verb root',null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20209,'pc-l21',5,'vocab','Also in this lesson',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
  (20210,'pc-l21',6,'vocab',null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null),
